# Even better: use one explicitly managed Letta App Server

For Moltwork production, I would actually stop using SDK-owned `local` mode in this HTTP service.

Run one Letta server:

```bash
letta server --backend local --listen ws://127.0.0.1:4500
```

That is the official self-hosted pattern. ([GitHub][5])

Then runtime-letta uses:

```ts
const client = new LettaAgentClient({
  backend: "remote",
  url: "http://127.0.0.1:4500",
});
```

Now:

```text
systemd/supervisor
      │
      ├── Letta App Server
      │      one process
      │
      └── Moltwork runtime-letta
             one process
```

No hidden subprocess lifecycle.

And because the App Server runs on the same host, its built-in `Read`/`Write`/`Bash` tools operate on that machine's campaign worktrees. Letta explicitly documents that remote built-in tools operate where the harness/App Server runs. ([GitHub][6])

This is probably the right permanent deployment.

